    "title": "What is a provider in Flutter, and how do you use it?",
    "answer": "Provider is a state management library in Flutter that allows you to share data between widgets efficiently and in a way that is easy to maintain. It works by providing a single source of truth for your app’s state, which can be accessed by any widget in your app. To use Provider, you typically define a ChangeNotifier class that represents your app’s state, and then wrap your app’s widgets in a ChangeNotifierProvider widget to make the state available to the widgets.",
