    "title": "What is Flutter’s rendering pipeline, and how does it work?",
    "answer": "Flutter’s rendering pipeline is responsible for updating the UI of a Flutter app. It works by first building a widget tree based on the current state of the app. Then, the engine uses the widget tree to generate a RenderObject tree, which is a low-level representation of the UI elements. Finally, the engine draws the UI by traversing the RenderObject tree and generating the necessary graphics commands.",
