    "title": "What is Flutter’s architecture, and how does it compare to other app development architectures?",
    "answer": "Flutter’s architecture is based on the BLoC pattern, which emphasizes the separation of concerns between the UI and the business logic. Compared to other app development architectures such as Model-View-Controller (MVC) or Model-View-Presenter (MVP), Flutter’s architecture provides a more modern, reactive approach to building apps. It is well-suited for building large and complex apps that require a lot of state management and data processing.",
